      "body": "Fixes the MoE GPU-count calculation and two errors in the Mistral launch arguments, plus documentation typos across six files.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Replace `TP × PP × CP × EP × DP` with separate attention (`TP × CP × PP × DP`) and expert (`EP × ETP × PP × EDP`) GPU-count formulas. Define the parallelism dimensions, explain how DP and EDP are derived, and link to the MoE documentation.\n- Fix the missing continuation backslash after `--attention-softmax-in-fp32` and correct `--disable-bia-linear` to `--disable-bias-linear` in the Mistral instructions.\n- Correct the documentation build guide's reference from NeMo RL to Megatron Core.\n- Fix wording in the fusion guide and capitalization, hyphenation, and spacing in the BERT and GPT API guides.\n\n## Formula scope\n\nThe GPU-count formulas describe standard MoE parallel folding with GTP/EGTP rematerialization factors set to 1. Configurations with larger rematerialization factors require accounting for those additional dimensions.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Compared all six changed files with upstream `main` at `07046cc6b8b7479ba05e6b47ed25f3f8e6634573`; the issues addressed by this PR remain present.\n- Checked the parallelism formulas against process-group initialization for the standard configuration.\n- Documentation-only changes; no training or runtime tests were run for this refresh.\n",
